preConditionHook:
// The pullback since the breakout has never traded back into the breakout
// bar: the lowest low of the last testWindow bars (INCLUSIVE of this one) is
// at or above the high of the bar testWindow bars ago, which stands in for the
// breakout bar. A fixed window rather than a persisted breakout-bar high, so
// the rule carries no state across bars.
//
// Both loops mirror EasyLanguage's Extremes(), which Highest()/Lowest() call:
// seeded at bar 0, scanning bars 1..Length-1, strict comparison so a tie keeps
// the earliest bar. Extremes is EL SOURCE, so its comparison carries the EL
// relational tolerance -- el_gt/el_lt, as in Breakout (the reference). Both
// sides are computed unconditionally: EasyLanguage does not short-circuit and
// Max Bars Back must cover testWindow on every bar regardless.
windowLow = low[0];
windowHigh = high[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)testWindow; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], windowLow)) windowLow = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], windowHigh)) windowHigh = high[i];
}
